+Generation first samples balanced quadratic-residue bucket classes from the
+public keys.  It gives each vertex a uniformly permuted local label block, sets
+its planted label to the bucket position, and only then samples edges between
+different buckets.  For an edge uv, t(uv)={0, |block(u)-block(v)|*stride}; this
+forbids exactly equal local positions and therefore proves the planted witness
+without search.  A random valid spanning path makes G connected.  The classes
+and all local blocks use the same marginal distributions.  Degree-residue,
+left-to-right greedy, 32 random greedy restarts, and every affine key ansatz are
+tested as attacks.  The exact DSATUR solver is kept out of attacks, as required
+for Track B, and its node/operation/wall-clock costs are measured.
