README.md:19:The Track-B claim is deliberately narrower than an average-case hardness claim.  Section 3, Theorem 1 gives `Solve-GLTC` in `O*((tau+2)^n)` time; storing predecessor transitions recovers a labeling.  The Introduction separately notes `O*(2^n)` for the all-`t(e)={0}` list-coloring case.  Section 3.1 improves the general bound for bounded degree, regular/claw-free, `K_1,d`-free and unit-disk graphs, and graphs with large clique packings.  This family does not claim to evade those algorithms.  Its executable exact DSATUR reference has worst-case `O(q^n(n+m))` cost and solved 8/8 shipping seeds at a median 12,658 nodes, 1,109,063 counted operations, and 0.890 seconds.  After recognizing the key invariant, the compact route takes 256 integer arithmetic operations.
