/tmp/tmp.HvTNsoPGLZ/gltc-arxiv2.tex:90:All the problems mentioned above are NP-complete for general graphs and remain so for many restricted graph classes. Therefore the generalized list $T$-coloring problem is NP-complete as well. When dealing with an NP-hard problem, there is little hope to design an exact algorithm,  running in polynomial time. Therefore we try to design exact exponential algorithm with exponential factor in the complexity bound as small as possible.
