+This module instantiates the exact object in Junosza-Szaniawski and Rzążewski, [“An Exact Algorithm for the Generalized List T-Coloring Problem”](https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.0603).  The solver receives a graph whose vertices have public integer keys, a finite permitted-label list for every vertex, and a forbidden set of absolute label differences for every edge.  It must return one permitted label per vertex while avoiding every forbidden edge difference.  The keys are vertex names carrying the compact-route clue, not an extra validity constraint. Verification is a direct exact scan of the lists and edges.
 
