Implemented a native Track B generalized list \(T\)-coloring generator based on the paper’s exact definition and \(O^*((\tau+2)^n)\) algorithm. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1311.0603)

Key deliverables:

- [gen_1311_0603.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1311.0603/gen_1311_0603.py:36)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1311.0603/selftest_report.json:1)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1311.0603/README.md:1)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1311.0603/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1311.0603/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1311.0603/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local verification passes all gates:

- 0 valid guesses in 200,000 structure-aware samples.
- Five attacks—including spectral clustering—succeeded 0/8.
- Exact DSATUR succeeded 8/8, with median 1,109,063 counted operations.
- 120/120 canonical-key symmetry checks passed.
- Answer: 245 characters, 64 elements; intended route: 256 operations.

The sole blocker is external: every mandatory OpenRouter call returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” Consequently, there are zero usable oracle attempts and no valid Step 4 hardness verdict. `submit.sh` correctly remains blocked. After restoring OpenRouter quota, rerun the bare, hinted, and placebo harness commands documented in the README.
